# Shell scripts must check out LF on every platform. build.yml runs
# scripts/release-notes.sh on the windows-latest runner, where Git for Windows'
# installer default (core.autocrlf=true) would hand bash a CRLF copy — which dies on
# `set -o pipefail` with "invalid option name" and, under `shell: bash` (errexit), fails
# the Windows leg and so skips publish-release for every release.
*.sh text eol=lf
